80\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T03:22:45-07:00","id":1540339,"title":"","content":"Well, with the Contagion Chronicle, it have 8 faction that is completing for the various Supernatural Population for it manpower, it would be kind of hard to imagine how big these faction are without knowing how big the population for each of the supernatural type to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T04:36:59-07:00","id":1540341,"title":"","content":"Sure! I just always took it that a city contains whatever population you need. It's a bit like the old 1 vampire per 100,000 people thing that fans used to fixate on. I never understood why it was important, unless you want to run a game where the focus is on a city being able to sustain that many Kindred or being overstretched. But I appreciate I'm not the target audience for your post, and appreciate it's of interest to you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T04:47:24-07:00","id":1540342,"title":"","content":"I alway feel like 1 every 100,000 is a very low number, especially when it's a world wide thing, there is only like 60,000 or so Vampire in the 2000s, strench all over the world, with 13 clan and various faction, it alway felt so small, when it was suppose to be big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T09:02:34-07:00","id":1540359,"title":"","content":"I think, like most people around here, I've never put down solid numbers like this.<br /> <br /> Among other issues, it goes way too hard in the opposite direction where instead of the supernatural being far too rare for what the books describe, the supernatural and supernaturally aware humans are over half of the world's population. The setting doesn't really work as intended if half of everyone walking down the street is some sort of supernaturally connected individual.<br /> <br /> One of the really good things the CofD did, is it made &quot;global&quot; numbers inconsequential. For every city with a few thousand vampires living in it, there's a city of equal size with zero vampires in it in favor of other things (or some mystery of why there's no supernatural presence at all!); and most of the splats have reason to gather that override things like relative populations to human residents (ex: Mages congregate around persistent Mysteries).<br /> <br /> Even using the Contagion Chronicle you're not doing a worldwide survey where these sorts of numbers are ever going to come up. If you want 5K werewolves operating in an area, and you want to stick to the broad strokes of the books, just give a reason for so many in such a small place (the books offer plenty of options). The Uratha are not in fact evenly distributed across the globe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T09:15:14-07:00","id":1540361,"title":"","content":"Another reason I have a population detail on each of the gameline Splat is because of a Chronicle idea I have, it's use rule from Mirror Infinite Macabre, Bleeding Edge, the Contagion Chronicle, and both Conspiracy rule from Deviant and Dominion rule from Exalted 2e Mandate of Heaven, which have been heavy rework to fit with Chronicle of Darkness. In the years 1991 both the Sworn and the False discover a way to cross into a dimension that they choose to call &quot;Celestial Realm&quot; it's like a mini universe, with 21 know galaxies, each with 200 Star System. And the realm have a curious trait in that, the Contagion can't spread here, it can't infect the realm, those who are infected with the Contagion can't enter the realm. And the law of this realm is very different from our own, you can breath in space but the air is kind of thin, and in certain section of space dangerous or cause strange effect, the star doesn't cause vampire to burn, while they're outside of a celestial body, but when on one, they start to burn, but slower and less intense that our sun. Now the Sworn and False battle both on Earth and in the Celestial Realm, for survival on Earth, and for glory in Celestial Realm. The Sworn is now an alliance between 5 Celestial Empire, which inculde the Cryptocracy Republic, which is a Republic and the most 'safe' and heavy guarded out of the 5 Empire. The Jeremiad Empire, which is a Theocracy with 10,000 religions all struggling for power and control over the Empire, but each give powerful blessing. The Rosetta Celestial Society, which is a Feudal Monarchy, they have thousand of archive full of culture and knowledge from all every culture in the Celestial Realm. The Ship of Theseus Collective which is a Oligarchy, they're the most technologically advance out of the Sworn, but also have the least amount of population, military, cultural identity, and goverment stability. And finally The Zero Hour Imperial, is a Stratocracy, they have the military of the alliance keeping the False faction at bay and far away from any of the Federation colonies. The False are lesser in number and have no alliance to each other, but thrive from the vastness of the Celestial Realm to hide from the Sworn Federation. The Crucible Ark, is a Democracy, they live on their giant space ships call Ark, plundering countless world of it natural resource for it Arks. The Machiavelli Coporation, is a Megacorp that exploit the various native alien nation for it own benefit, and pitting them against the Sworn Federation and each other. The Naglfar Pirate, is a intergalactic pirate group, that plunder the Sworn Federation, the other False, and native alien nations, they're very accepting for those wish to join them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T16:55:02-07:00","id":1540394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540359#post1540359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among other issues, it goes way too hard in the opposite direction where instead of the supernatural being far too rare for what the books describe, the supernatural and supernaturally aware humans are over half of the world's population. The setting doesn't really work as intended if half of everyone walking down the street is some sort of supernaturally connected individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's too much, the world is a big place, only around or so 20% of the World of Population is Supernatural and 30% of the World population know the Supernatural exist, which isn't a lot when you consider how much the population of the Supernatural and the aware Mortal are actually in any given area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T17:54:26-07:00","id":1540397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540394#post1540394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's too much, the world is a big place, only around or so 20% of the World of Population is Supernatural and 30% of the World population know the Supernatural exist, which isn't a lot when you consider how much the population of the Supernatural and the aware Mortal are actually in any given area.</div> </div> </div> </div>A quarter of the world's population is not older than the age of 14. You've here given global Promethean numbers that are several <i>dozen </i>times the rough estimate put forth in 2e, not to mention put per-subsplat numbers for multiple monster-types high enough to outnumber the tenth most populous city in the most populous country in the world not named India or China. You've got more of the rumored Nuclear Prometheans than people possessed by Infernal demons despite Prometheans being rare and Zeky being rare enough that most Prometheans haven't encountered one, more Beasts than mages when Beasts are explicitly outnumbered by mages, and numbers for rare variant werewolf auspices but no numbers for the primary antagonistic werewolf faction. Even if one treats &quot;being a supernatural entity&quot; and &quot;being aware of the supernatural&quot; as equivalent despite the bluebook Integrity question establishing basically anyone who's a player character has had some exposure to the supernatural that they try not to think about, these numbers are still kinda weird.<br /> <br /> I tend to take the view that playable monsters being accorded the same level of narrative importance as named sub-leaders in tokusatsu-archetypical evil organizations entails a similar degree of scarcity \u2014 there aren't going to be enough in an area to credibly treat any of them as faceless background characters without circumstances dramatically ratcheting up their density on the ground, like the mass gatherings of Prometheans in New Orleans and Boston in the 1e's Water of Life chronicle. My own Changeling chronicle plays slightly fast and loose with its local numbers by virtue of the freehold being sponsored by a couple Agencies of demons experimenting with fae Covers while observing a metaphysical gas leak, but I'd still be hard-pressed to put its total non-Integrity-bearing headcount in the triple digits altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T18:23:59-07:00","id":1540403,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it kind of weird, I didn't know Mage outnumbered Beast, I orignally have Beast at only 10,000 per family, but felt it was too little. I have the Possessed be at 666, because it the number of the devil, and I remember it was the number of the Lucifurge. I have Promethean be in the 1,000 because, it's a big world, a few hundred feel too little to me, 7,777 Promethean is nothing compare to the 8.2 billion people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T18:27:54-07:00","id":1540405,"title":"","content":"Well with Changelings in our city we had at best 100 permanent members and roughly at best 200 Mages in the city and a few dozen in the nearby regions. But we never stopped to consider what the worldwide population was for any of the groups. Realistically in regards to Vampires in our city we felt that at best 30 was a good number and maybe 5 or 6 were old enough to be consider elders or ancillea of any decent blood potency and the rest were a mixture of older and young neonates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-15-2024, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T18:51:36-07:00","id":1540408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540361#post1540361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...A lot of Space Opera stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea, even if not my favorite I can appreciate some Space Opera twists on the setting<br /> <br /> But what this have to do with the numbers?<br /> <br /> You don't only have very weird numbers for the world population, I'm still unconvinced that this is at all necessary for your setting.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite. With a whole new universe to occupy unimpeded, I see the supernatural numbers on Earth being all the more fluid, and probably diminished, as many have now 4200 star systems to live in outside our world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T19:13:13-07:00","id":1540409,"title":"","content":"Well, they would only get access to the Celestial Realm if they either join the Sworn or the False faction, and I don't think every supernatural person want to live life fighting the Contagion or the False.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T18:05:52-07:00","id":1540485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540409#post1540409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they would only get access to the Celestial Realm if they either join the Sworn or the False faction, and I don't think every supernatural person want to live life fighting the Contagion or the False.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the point.<br /> <br /> It's still more fluid. It still makes your numbers more strange.<br /> <br /> And I'm still unconvinced that this was necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T18:49:01-07:00","id":1540491,"title":"","content":"Maybe it wasn't necessary, but I find it more convienent to know the exact or close enough number of the Supernatural population in my game. And know how much their population loss is going to affect that splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T19:03:15-07:00","id":1540492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540409#post1540409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they would only get access to the Celestial Realm if they either join the Sworn or the False faction, and I don't think every supernatural person want to live life fighting the Contagion or the False.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must confess <i>extreme</i> confusion over how you square the circle of &quot;you only get access to the mini-universe where the Contagion can't get in if you join one of the factions that are explicitly fighting the Contagion, who are for some reason also spreading intergalactically in that Contagion-free mini-universe far and wide enough to still clash with one-another in any meaningful sense.&quot; Are there just a lot of aliens that present their own problems? Given that the perspectives of the False and the fact that they all share the Contagion Vector, what point is there in their continued existence as factions in the Celestial Realm and/or lingering in the established setting? Why have the factions dedicated enough resources to attaining something resembling intergalactic statehood while still ostensibly caring about a problem that explicitly cannot affect the space those states exist in? Are the numbers provided in the original post of this thread distributed across those hundreds of star systems, or are those several billion monsters concentrated into a much smaller subset of planets in this setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T11:05:56-07:00","id":1540519,"title":"","content":"My question is about the intentions of some of the suggested numbers. Why are werewolves by far the most numerous of them? Why are Changelings and Unchained second to that, and still by that metric still vastly outnumbering the likes of mages?<br /> <br /> I think perspectives on approximate sizes for populations of supernaturals relative to one another, and to the world at large, should be modelled on things like the kinds of activities they undertake and the sorts of societies attributed to them, as well as what might be expected from their origins. I wouldn't buy mages as one of the smaller populations because they have one of the more elaborate and internationally connected social structures. Nor would I think Demons and Changelings are so numerous, both because it runs counters to their particular themes of living in secrecy even within the occult underground, and undermines the credibility of what they had to overcome to be at large in the world.<br /> <br /> Uratha I actually do think myself of as the most numerous, but not to that extent where it seems as though they'd be crowding one another out a bit and, importantly, where the rate of incidents where any of them rage out of control seems as though it should have a big visible impact.<br /> <br /> 20% might sound sufficient because it's a minority, but I think it's worth breaking down just how big of a minority it is. Like, just think about what it would mean if statistically any given visit to something like a shopping mall means you're sharing the space with dozens of supernatural people.<br /> <br /> Conversely, the fact that the overall population is huge means that you can get by with all supernaturals combined constituting a much smaller percentage overall and still have a very large number of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T11:28:26-07:00","id":1540522,"title":"","content":"The reason I put Mage population be low is because they're very powerful, and I heard that Awakening are very rare. Changeling are big, because story of fairy are a lot more common than Vampire or Mage. And the reason there so many Demon is because there is so many Angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T13:33:07-07:00","id":1540527,"title":"","content":"Has this question popped up again?<br /> <br /> I've spent time thinking about this, mostly for fun. It's almost never going to be relevant in a game (unless you're doing something like a Werewolf: the Apocalypse end times scenario), but thinking about rough proportions can help me build settings.<br /> <br /> Like vampires congregate, and have traditionally needed decent numbers to keep up their organisational structures. So I estimate that anywhere important enough to set a Chronicle probably has one vampire per ten thousand people, even if the actual global population is lower by an order of magnitude or more.<br /> <br /> Werewolves? Who knows. There's somewhere between thousands and millions worldwide, and the number fluctuates wildly over the decades. There's a handful of packs around here, but that's all we know.<br /> <br /> With Mages global population is more of a concern, as they can communicate across the world even in ye olde dayes before the telegraph. At which point theoretically reasonable numbers like one in a million start to give you far too many mages. There are likely maybe a few thousand in the world, and people are currently awakening proportionally less than they did but there's still more total mages than before.<br /> <br /> Changelings? Up to hundreds per freehold, and they pop up in the weirdest places.<br /> <br /> Deviants? Nobody knows, but the Renegades in your country probably number in the tens.<br /> <br /> Mummies? Maybe as few as a thousand in the entire world. Today most have been moved to the US or China, but not every Cult wants to risk moving the death god.<br /> <br /> Hunters? Kind of a moot question as someone is always taking up or dropping the Vigil. But one in a million is not a bad guess for the worldwide population.<br /> <br /> Other splats? I don't own those books","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T20:26:36-07:00","id":1540547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540527#post1540527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has this question popped up again?<br /> <br /> I've spent time thinking about this, mostly for fun. It's almost never going to be relevant in a game (unless you're doing something like a Werewolf: the Apocalypse end times scenario), but thinking about rough proportions can help me build settings.<br /> <br /> Like vampires congregate, and have traditionally needed decent numbers to keep up their organisational structures. So I estimate that anywhere important enough to set a Chronicle probably has one vampire per ten thousand people, even if the actual global population is lower by an order of magnitude or more.<br /> <br /> Werewolves? Who knows. There's somewhere between thousands and millions worldwide, and the number fluctuates wildly over the decades. There's a handful of packs around here, but that's all we know.<br /> <br /> With Mages global population is more of a concern, as they can communicate across the world even in ye olde dayes before the telegraph. At which point theoretically reasonable numbers like one in a million start to give you far too many mages. There are likely maybe a few thousand in the world, and people are currently awakening proportionally less than they did but there's still more total mages than before.<br /> <br /> Changelings? Up to hundreds per freehold, and they pop up in the weirdest places.<br /> <br /> Deviants? Nobody knows, but the Renegades in your country probably number in the tens.<br /> <br /> Mummies? Maybe as few as a thousand in the entire world. Today most have been moved to the US or China, but not every Cult wants to risk moving the death god.<br /> <br /> Hunters? Kind of a moot question as someone is always taking up or dropping the Vigil. But one in a million is not a bad guess for the worldwide population.<br /> <br /> Other splats? I don't own those books</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are your number so low? There are definetly more Deviant than ten thousand Deviant in given country, given how big the Web of Pain is, and what the theme of the game is going for.<br /> <br /> And Hunter only being one in a million doesn't even make sense, because there're officially at the very least, more than 10,000 Hunter, and becoming a Hunter is easier than any other splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T01:21:58-07:00","id":1540554,"title":"","content":"The numbers are low because most of us care more about the themes of the setting (default: urban fantasy horror where there supernatural is very real, but also hidden and that being hidden part requires lower numbers broadly speaking to make any sense).<br /> <br /> There's a point where these threads are kinda pointless if you're running your games so divorced from what the primary focus of the games are that those of us running more default games have experiences that just aren't going to mean anything to what you're doing at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T02:36:58-07:00","id":1540557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540547#post1540547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why are your number so low? There are definetly more Deviant than ten thousand Deviant in given country, given how big the Web of Pain is, and what the theme of the game is going for.<br /> <br /> And Hunter only being one in a million doesn't even make sense, because there're officially at the very least, more than 10,000 Hunter, and becoming a Hunter is easier than any other splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The numbers are low for multiple reasons:<br /> 1) I'm trying to keep human-derived supernaturals far below 1% of the population.<br /> 2) for many I've stuck to local populations. This is especially true for Changelings, where I'm assuming freeholds can be anywhere and that cities aren't limited to one (and some have none).<br /> 3) these numbers are designed around themes, there's so few Renegades running around because not only were they rare to begin with they regularly die or get captured. Renegades are supposed to be isolated.<br /> <br /> As for hunters I'd honestly just forgotten that the world population is in short form and was working in long form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T02:54:44-07:00","id":1540558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540557#post1540557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) these numbers are designed around themes, there's so few Renegades running around because not only were they rare to begin with they regularly die or get captured. Renegades are supposed to be isolated.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true for a Renegade Chronicle, but you also got to think of the Devoted Chronicle where you expected to see a lot more Deviant, either by hunting down Renegade, dealing with other Conspiracy, or making new Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T04:43:36-07:00","id":1540560,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't care to plot out specific numbers, but if someone put a gun to my head I'd say about 1% of the world having something supernatural about them, and half of those being a supernatural merit is where I would start. Having half the world in the know completely shatters any hope or need for secrecy, it could be a very good, true blood esque game, but it's not what I think of as the default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T06:27:44-07:00","id":1540566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540560#post1540560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't care to plot out specific numbers, but if someone put a gun to my head I'd say about 1% of the world having something supernatural about them, and half of those being a supernatural merit is where I would start. Having half the world in the know completely shatters any hope or need for secrecy, it could be a very good, true blood esque game, but it's not what I think of as the default.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could work in a comedic game where each group is completely taken in by the other's masquerades.<br /> <br /> Otherwise? LGBTQIA+ people compromise like 10% of the population, and we've never successfully hidden our existence as a group even during the most homophobic times. I don't see any way for a significant proportion of the population to be supernatural without causing enough hunters to make it common knowledge.<br /> <br /> 1% is, I feel, a good compromise figure. It lets you keep the CofD idea that most people have encountered the supernatural, but it's low enough that few people have had meaningful interactions with it. Those that do tend to end up with a minor template or have some kind of supernatural merit themselves (particularly Aura Reading).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T12:07:55-07:00","id":1540582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540522#post1540522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I put Mage population be low is because they're very powerful</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, I don't think they're powerful in a way that making them more numerous would cause some kind of overwhelming effect (setting aside a point that at any given time, the majority of mages are probably at Disciple level in Arcana).<br /> <br /> Awakening is uncommon, sure (which is why I imagine mage numbers are still on the low end of the big three supernatural groups), but I don't think to an extent that necessarily leaves their population extremely low.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling are big, because story of fairy are a lot more common than Vampire or Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what bearing does that have? It's not as if changelings are going to be the foundation of all fairy folklore, and even if they were that's an issue for the past to deal with. The big constraint of the Lost is that they need to escape from the clutches of their kidnappers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the reason there so many Demon is because there is so many Angel.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Are</i> there lots of angels?<br /> <br /> Even if there were, the conditions that lead to them attaining true free will strike me as some of the most unlikely to occur of all. I think it's a way bigger break away from your pre-existing pattern than something like Awakening is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T13:09:50-07:00","id":1540587,"title":"","content":"I think that having supernatural beings being only 1% of the total population of Earth makes good sense and helps sells there secret societies more effectively. In our city the Changeling and Mage population don't even make 1% of 1% of the local population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T14:31:29-07:00","id":1540590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540582#post1540582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakening is uncommon, sure (which is why I imagine mage numbers are still on the low end of the big three supernatural groups), but I don't think to an extent that necessarily leaves their population extremely low.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notably, it's more explicit that <i>successful</i> Awakening is uncommon, albeit even an unsuccessful Awakening still produces a Sleepwalker and every mage of the appropriate Path can detect an Awakening in progress at a minimum range measured in miles, but yeah,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well what bearing does that have? It's not as if changelings are going to be the foundation of all fairy folklore, and even if they were that's an issue for the past to deal with. The big constraint of the Lost is that they need to escape from the clutches of their kidnappers. </div> </div> </div>By way of addendum, the tendency/capacity for supernatural beings to sever ties with their old mortal lives and/or assume a new identity means 1e's old assessment that changeling populations tend to be higher in places where lots of people come and go probably has some weight. (The bigger concern for global changeling population being the involvement of a whole extradimensional axis the Lost can hide in that doesn't have a concrete scale.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Are</i> there lots of angels?<br /> <br /> Even if there were, the conditions that lead to them attaining true free will strike me as some of the most unlikely to occur of all. I think it's a way bigger break away from your pre-existing pattern than something like Awakening is. </div> </div> </div>Demon is a little hazy on this, but the corebook notes that &quot;most&quot; occult matrices involve an angel and that the God-Machine's recycling processes mean most of the angels who become demons managed to harbor and hide their doubts long enough to break their connection within the timeframe of a single mission. Given that angel-jacking to steal a new Cover tends to be at least a minor heist in practice, that suggests the narrative pacing of introducing new angels locally seldom happens more than a few times per story, especially since the Machine prefers to use mundane methods for its plans where possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T18:30:22-07:00","id":1540601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540491#post1540491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it wasn't necessary, but I find it more convienent to know the exact or close enough number of the Supernatural population in my game. And know how much their population loss is going to affect that splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are those numbers just for the Earth, or are they for the whole Earth + Miniature Universe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T08:19:36-07:00","id":1540626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540492#post1540492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must confess <i>extreme</i> confusion over how you square the circle of &quot;you only get access to the mini-universe where the Contagion can't get in if you join one of the factions that are explicitly fighting the Contagion, who are for some reason also spreading intergalactically in that Contagion-free mini-universe far and wide enough to still clash with one-another in any meaningful sense.&quot; Are there just a lot of aliens that present their own problems?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of alien within the Celestial Realm, and some are more hostile than other. There're many Space Empire already exisiting within the Celestial Realm, but aren't any within the Galaxy that the Sworn and False start in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540492#post1540492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the perspectives of the False and the fact that they all share the Contagion Vector, what point is there in their continued existence as factions in the Celestial Realm and/or lingering in the established setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>The False still exist because their philosophy still matter, the Crucible Initiative still exist because they think it only a matter of time before the Contagion spread to this Realm, and with the existence of Anomalous Mutation and the Immunites they have evidence to back up their worry. So they decide to live in fleet constantly travelling the Realm, extracting resource from System to System, avoiding Anomalous Zone, and exterminate any Immunite and Mutant that come their way.<br /> The Machiavelli Gambit still exist because they now have even more pawn to control with and new asset to manage, they now manage the Anomalous Mutation instead of the Contagion, and use the various Empire and Immunite armies to their advantage. Naglfar Army want Monster to still exist, and the Celestial Realm is big obstacle in their goal, the Immunite and Anomalous Mutation are enough evidence from them to think that their existence is in danger, they now plunder the Realm Empire, keeping Monster alive. Obviously the Contagion Vector have been change a bit to work within Realm that have no Contagion, instead it now work by manipulating Anomalous Mutation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540492#post1540492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why have the factions dedicated enough resources to attaining something resembling intergalactic statehood while still ostensibly caring about a problem that explicitly cannot affect the space those states exist in?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sworn and False are still interested in Earth because of the Celestial Realm connection to Earth, while the Contagion can't enter the Celestial Realm, it can affect it in other way, causing Anomalous Mutation and Immunite. Anomalous Mutation happen, when the Contagion is affecting Earth, Anomalous Mutation have 4 stage, with varying degree of size and intensity, it can range from a planet wide Mutation to a whole galaxy, Anomalous Mutation only affect the environment, which both have a benefit and a drawback. Immunites are extra-dimensional species, that are very durable, adaptable, and deadly, they come out of Worlds Wound, which happen when Anomalous Mutation exist for a long enough period of time without curing it Contagion mutagen. Immunites only goal is to destroy everything in the Celestial Realm, and they have multiple specialize version, can regenerate very fast, and there're are almost endless amount of them, so that why both the Sworn and the False can't send all of their manpower to invade Earth. To stop the Anomalous Mutation from growing and getting more mutated, they must cure the Contagion that cause the Anomalous Mutation in the first place, after curing the Contagion, Anomalous Mutation will stop growing and mutation, and it drawback become lessen or stop having drawback all together, this also cause Worlds Wound to start the healing process. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540492#post1540492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the numbers provided in the original post of this thread distributed across those hundreds of star systems, or are those several billion monsters concentrated into a much smaller subset of planets in this setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>The number provide in the original post are the total Population of both Earth and the Celestial Realm, each of the faction only have one system that is fully colonize, the rest are just colonies for specific purpose.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T08:48:07-07:00","id":1540628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540626#post1540626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are a lot of alien within the Celestial Realm, and some are more hostile than other. There're many Space Empire already exisiting within the Celestial Realm, but aren't any within the Galaxy that the Sworn and False start in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The False still exist because their philosophy still matter, the Crucible Initiative still exist because they think it only a matter of time before the Contagion spread to this Realm, and with the existence of Anomalous Mutation and the Immunites they have evidence to back up their worry. So they decide to live in fleet constantly travelling the Realm, extracting resource from System to System, avoiding Anomalous Zone, and exterminate any Immunite and Mutant that come their way.<br /> The Machiavelli Gambit still exist because they now have even more pawn to control with and new asset to manage, they now manage the Anomalous Mutation instead of the Contagion, and use the various Empire and Immunite armies to their advantage. Naglfar Army want Monster to still exist, and the Celestial Realm is big obstacle in their goal, the Immunite and Anomalous Mutation are enough evidence from them to think that their existence is in danger, they now plunder the Realm Empire, keeping Monster alive. Obviously the Contagion Vector have been change a bit to work within Realm that have no Contagion, instead it now work by manipulating Anomalous Mutation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Sworn and False are still interested in Earth because of the Celestial Realm connection to Earth, while the Contagion can't enter the Celestial Realm, it can affect it in other way, causing Anomalous Mutation and Immunite. Anomalous Mutation happen, when the Contagion is affecting Earth, Anomalous Mutation have 4 stage, with varying degree of size and intensity, it can range from a planet wide Mutation to a whole galaxy, Anomalous Mutation only affect the environment, which both have a benefit and a drawback. Immunites are extra-dimensional species, that are very durable, adaptable, and deadly, they come out of Worlds Wound, which happen when Anomalous Mutation exist for a long enough period of time without curing it Contagion mutagen. Immunites only goal is to destroy everything in the Celestial Realm, and they have multiple specialize version, can regenerate very fast, and there're are almost endless amount of them, so that why both the Sworn and the False can't send all of their manpower to invade Earth. To stop the Anomalous Mutation from growing and getting more mutated, they must cure the Contagion that cause the Anomalous Mutation in the first place, after curing the Contagion, Anomalous Mutation will stop growing and mutation, and it drawback become lessen or stop having drawback all together, this also cause Worlds Wound to start the healing process.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The number provide in the original post are the total Population of both Earth and the Celestial Realm, each of the faction only have one system that is fully colonize, the rest are just colonies for specific purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's still hard to believe these factions would care about the realm so much to waste resources on it when earth is suffering far worse. Why care about a seemingly immune system when patient 0 (the main reality) is the one suffering the disease?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T14:02:31-07:00","id":1540655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540626#post1540626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sworn and False are still interested in Earth because of the Celestial Realm connection to Earth, while the Contagion can't enter the Celestial Realm, it can affect it in other way, causing Anomalous Mutation and Immunite. Anomalous Mutation happen, when the Contagion is affecting Earth, Anomalous Mutation have 4 stage, with varying degree of size and intensity, it can range from a planet wide Mutation to a whole galaxy, Anomalous Mutation only affect the environment, which both have a benefit and a drawback. Immunites are extra-dimensional species, that are very durable, adaptable, and deadly, they come out of Worlds Wound, which happen when Anomalous Mutation exist for a long enough period of time without curing it Contagion mutagen. Immunites only goal is to destroy everything in the Celestial Realm, and they have multiple specialize version, can regenerate very fast, and there're are almost endless amount of them, so that why both the Sworn and the False can't send all of their manpower to invade Earth. To stop the Anomalous Mutation from growing and getting more mutated, they must cure the Contagion that cause the Anomalous Mutation in the first place, after curing the Contagion, Anomalous Mutation will stop growing and mutation, and it drawback become lessen or stop having drawback all together, this also cause Worlds Wound to start the healing process.</div> </div> </div> </div>This\u2026 sounds like a roundabout way of saying that the Contagion <i>can</i> enter the Celestial Realm, if it causes Anomalous Mutations whose severity eventually rips holes in reality from which near-endless forces of destruction emerge.<br /> <br /> Does the Celestial Realm have its own Shadow, Underworld, Hedge, God-Machine, etc? If so, are they similarly separated from their Earthly counterparts? If not, is it functionally just a parallel world that works like the material world except where noted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The number provide in the original post are the total Population of both Earth and the Celestial Realm, each of the faction only have one system that is fully colonize, the rest are just colonies for specific purpose. </div> </div> </div>What year is it on Earth in this setting and (if there is a time differential between universes) how long have the factions been active in the Celestial Realm? Breathable vacuum notwithstanding, how are they managing interstellar travel? Are there just multiple points of Earthly entry to the Celestial Realm that come out in different galaxies? Do those existing space empires have any difficulty getting to Earth? Are their peoples and creatures immune to the Contagion's non-Celestial manifestations? Can parts of a world subject to an Anomalous Mutation cross over to Earth (and if so, is their higher scalar floor dialed down or is every instance of this happening a potentially apocalyptic threat)?<br /> <br /> Given the emphasis on factional jockeying and the general need to knowingly join one, wouldn't factional population numbers be more useful for this purpose than trying to pin down the demographics of a bunch of monsters that can make themselves very hard to find by virtue of invisibility, psychic misdirection, and/or extradimensional hidey-holes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T20:40:38-07:00","id":1540686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540655#post1540655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This\u2026 sounds like a roundabout way of saying that the Contagion <i>can</i> enter the Celestial Realm, if it causes Anomalous Mutations whose severity eventually rips holes in reality from which near-endless forces of destruction emerge.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not exactly like the Contagion, it only affect the environment, so you could just leave the Anomalous zone to not be affected by Anomalous Mutation, it can Mutate creature, but that only happen in Stage 3 and 4, and even then it's still rare, it can't be spread like the Contagion, and the mutation start to disappear after you leave the Anomalous Zone for long period of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540655#post1540655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Celestial Realm have its own Shadow, Underworld, Hedge, God-Machine, etc? If so, are they similarly separated from their Earthly counterparts? If not, is it functionally just a parallel world that works like the material world except where noted?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Celestial Realm have Astral Realm the Twilight, the Supernal Realm, and the Divine Fire, but the various Invisible Realm of Earth can be access through the Celestial Realm by mixing the Occult Technology that they use to open a gateway to the Celestial Realm, and the Supernatural ability to enter a paticular Realm, they can create a Key which can create gateway from the Celestial Realm to that Realm, that can only be open by that Key. Each Realm have a different type of Key, Underworld have actual key, the Shadow use talisman, the Hedge use mask, etc. While there is no God Machine in the Celestial Realm, there're strange and ancient Monument across the Realm that generate Aether. There're vast ancient ruin fill with relics and artifacts, that contain Sekham, and in the Celestial Realm it take double the time to make a Descent roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540655#post1540655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What year is it on Earth in this setting and (if there is a time differential between universes) how long have the factions been active in the Celestial Realm? Breathable vacuum notwithstanding, how are they managing interstellar travel? Are there just multiple points of Earthly entry to the Celestial Realm that come out in different galaxies? Do those existing space empires have any difficulty getting to Earth? Are their peoples and creatures immune to the Contagion's non-Celestial manifestations? Can parts of a world subject to an Anomalous Mutation cross over to Earth (and if so, is their higher scalar floor dialed down or is every instance of this happening a potentially apocalyptic threat)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Space Empire of the Celestial Realm don't know that Earth exist, before the Sworn and False discover the Celestial Realm, most of the empires were more focus on dealing with their own galaxy than exploring what outside of it, and the Galatic Portal were inactive, and it's only the decade that the Space Empires met the Sworn and False. There're alien species in the Celestial Realm that are more resistance against to certain kind of Contagion, but the Immunite are very resistance to the environmental effect of the Anomalous Mutation, and Immune to being infect with the Contagion. Anomalous Mutation can't get on Earth, because Earth reality isn't as mutable. It's 2025 on Earth and there is no time difference between Earth and this Realm. There're 3 way of traveling between the stars, using the Celestial Pathway, using Spaceship, or using Galactic Portal. Celestial Pathway is a pathway made of star, that let people cross between planet and star system that are within the same region of a galaxy. It's take hours to travel between planet within the same system, and day and even months to go to another system, Celestial Pathway can be travel by using boat, car, horse, and plane. There is no Celestial Pathway to cross from one region of a galaxy to the other, spaceship are use for that instead. Ship range from size to speed, they can travel between planet in matter of second to minutes to hours, system in minutes to hours to days, and traveling to another region in hours to days to months. But even the fastest ship can't travel between galaxies without it taking months, but that where Galactic Portal come in. Galactic Portal are found either on planet or in space, they allow for instant travel between planet, system, region, and galaxies, how big the Galatic Portal is depend on how far it's travelling, Galatic Portal are rare, so most people use Celestial Pathway and spaceship to travel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540655#post1540655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the emphasis on factional jockeying and the general need to knowingly join one, wouldn't factional population numbers be more useful for this purpose than trying to pin down the demographics of a bunch of monsters that can make themselves very hard to find by virtue of invisibility, psychic misdirection, and/or extradimensional hidey-holes?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, but I like to have a base for the faction population number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T20:42:27-07:00","id":1540687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540628#post1540628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it's still hard to believe these factions would care about the realm so much to waste resources on it when earth is suffering far worse. Why care about a seemingly immune system when patient 0 (the main reality) is the one suffering the disease?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a entire mini-universe with untap rich and resource, with no goverment to get that cut, or human you need to hide from. It a safe place where the Contagion can't infect you, it's vast, and full of mystery, there is lot of reason to invest in the colonization of the realm, especially when it could be the key to stopping the Contagion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T20:45:56-07:00","id":1540688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540687#post1540687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a entire mini-universe with untap rich and resource, with no goverment to get that cut, or human you need to hide from. It a safe place where the Contagion can't infect you, it's vast, and full of mystery, there is lot of reason to invest in the colonization of the realm, especially when it could be the key to stopping the Contagion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why not dedicate all resources to simply inhabiting it and cutting it from earth afterwards? Let the naglfars army have their way afterwards.<br /> <br /> That's ignoring that I don't see the Sworn or False being able get anywhere close to successfully navigating much less colonizing a mini universe on even the local level of a planet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T23:00:30-07:00","id":1540690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1540688#post1540688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why not dedicate all resources to simply inhabiting it and cutting it from earth afterwards? Let the naglfars army have their way afterwards.<br /> <br /> That's ignoring that I don't see the Sworn or False being able get anywhere close to successfully navigating much less colonizing a mini universe on even the local level of a planet</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there is the problem of Anomalous Mutation, Immunites, Hostile Alien Empire, Dangerous Alien Environment, and Strange Space Horror, that why they can't just put all of their resource to inhabiting the Realm, and also I think you misunderstand Naglfar Army goal.<br /> <br /> Why do you think the Sworn and False can't navigate and colonize the Celestial Realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T04:27:49-07:00","id":1543577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population#post1540330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that the book said the Population is as much as your story need but what is the actual population number in your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Earlier, I used to try to fit such numbers as well. But gradually, I realized that in my world, the populations would not be evenly distributed. I do not have numbers for all supernaturals, but for example for vampires, I came up with the following relation:<br /> <br /> vampires in the city = city population/(10000+17.82*sqrt(city population))<br /> <br /> where I would assume cities under 30k people would have 0 vampires. Averaged over all cities this leads to cca 1 in 35,000 in EU and 1 in 20,000 in the USA.<br /> <br /> The reasoning is following: vampires tend to live in the cities. If the cities are large, the Prince holding dominion over the city will probably want to regulate the vampire populations so that the problems do not grow over his head. But even a small city of, say 30,000 people might sustain a few vampires who are reasonably secretive. I would assume they would use the freedom of not being under a strict control of a prince in a large city.<br /> <br /> It also has a practical reason: I often play in Prague (1 million people), and I want to have non-trivial population in the city for the game to be interesting. On the other hand, if I would keep this ratio and play in large cities of 20 million people, there would be so many characters that my head would explode just thinking about the factions and interactions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T10:16:32-07:00","id":1543587,"title":"","content":"Not much that I can add in regards to Kindred population in large cities of a million or so. But having a number of two or three dozen seems reasonable as there would be enough hunting grounds and fiefdoms for smart vampires to be okay with and that the Prince would be able to maintain effective control and keep conflicts to a minimum.<br /> <br /> For small cities of 30,000-50,000 thousand it might be able to support at best 3 or 4 kindred who would have enough space to suit there needs.<br /> <br /> And it should be stressed that this urban fantasy and horror and of the ways to keep humans away is to keep numbers quite low and widespread and I use the Kelly Armstrong series of novels on the supernatural as a good guide to go by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  I got the name of a writer wrong. 10-12-2024, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T14:47:24-07:00","id":1543596,"title":"","content":"In fact when we were playing Mage The Awakening, we made sure to view it as urban fantasy and why magi practiced the arts quietly and how cabals would nudge mortal society to better the quality of the Awakened lives. Kelly Armstrong had a good couple of books that dealt with mages and how there society would run or even Stephen Blackmore's necromancer character and I bet some of us used Jim Butcher for ideas.<br /> <br /> I found it as a good source of inspiration for our old games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  I got a name wrong. 10-12-2024, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T21:41:04-07:00","id":1544624,"title":"","content":"I've played a lot of fantasy and cyberpunk games, I didn't scratch out one less orc or street-punk when they got toasted. <br /> <br /> I'd say, there are a lot of simple splats like psychics, Second-Sight people, etc. than major splats like vampires and werewolves. <br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires, it's feast of famine; I either have only a few, or the city is over-populated (In V:tM, I generally have less vamps; Requiem and Night's Edge, I have more; a lot more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-09T16:45:17-08:00","id":1547654,"title":"","content":"In my imagination, I always figured the following.<br /> <br /> Uratha about 500,000, simply because the first edition repeated it so many times, about 180,000 and 300,000 Pure<br /> <br /> Kindred, about 160,000 to 180,000, or 1 per 50,000 people<br /> <br /> Mages about 40,000<br /> <br /> Changelings about 20,000 because they did a population analysis in one of the books about Summer<br /> <br /> Promethians about 100 because the core book says so.<br /> <br /> Geist, not really any idea, but maybe the same as Changelings.<br /> <br /> Mummies, about 1,000 by doing a calculation with data from the first edition<br /> <br /> Demons, no idea, some tens of thousands?<br /> <br /> Beasts, no idea, some tens of thousands?<br /> <br /> Deviants, maybe more since there are so many conspiracies, maybe over 100,000, but fluctuating and most are the weaker kind<br /> <br /> Hunters, theoretically the Human race at 8 Billion, but more likely, maybe at any given time 1 in 10,000 humans is a hunter in a cell. This number can rise quickly if the supernatural creatures get sloppy and give humans a reason to load their shotguns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T06:56:41-08:00","id":1548090,"title":"","content":"I have a related question, which fits well into this thread, I think.<br /> <br /> What are the [Supernatural Stat] and [Discipline Levels] distributions of your populations in a city? For example, I have 10 mages in my Prague. How many of them would have what levels of Gnosis in your world? On what levels would be their Arcana? The same question for vampires or werewolves. Do you mostly keep the NPCs comparable to the starting players, like Gnosis / Blood Potency / Primal Urge 1-3? Or do you also have a significant population on 4-6, or even more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T10:14:58-08:00","id":1548094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540330-your-chronicle-of-darknesss-population?p=1548090#post1548090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, I have 10 mages in my Prague.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's a very small population, so it could go a few different ways depending on why it's like that.<br /> <br /> Like, did something wipe out a larger consilium? Maybe now the only mages are apprentices and disciples moving into the space created by the destruction?<br /> <br /> Or maybe there's a situation where a group of masters have just so locked down the magical resources of the city that no one else bothers (1e Boston was suggested to have been a bit like that in the past).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}